    "body": "Great feature! 🎉 This addresses a real need for splitting configurations across multiple files. However, I'm concerned about the custom TOML parser in `src/context.rs:507-531`. It fails with complex TOML structures like arrays:\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n# config1.toml\r\n[[battery.display]]\r\nthreshold = 10\r\nstyle = \"bold red\"\r\n\r\n# config2.toml  \r\n[[battery.display]]\r\nthreshold = 25\r\nstyle = \"bold yellow\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe current line-by-line parser can't handle `[[battery.display]]` syntax properly. Since Starship already uses `toml = \"0.9.5\"`, consider using `toml::from_str()` for parsing instead of the custom approach. This would handle arrays, nested tables, and multiline strings properly.",
    "state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED",
